# Refresh main in cloud environments

Cursor Cloud VMs often boot from a snapshot whose `main` is hours behind origin. Before branching or editing in a cloud session, update `main`. Skip this on a local checkout.

```sh
# ✅ GOOD — first commands in a cloud session
git fetch origin main
git checkout main
git pull --ff-only origin main
# then create the feature branch from that tip
```

```sh
# ❌ BAD — branch from the snapshot checkout
git checkout -b cursor/my-change
```

Retry fetch/pull on network errors (4s, 8s, 16s, 32s). Do not force-push or reset unrelated local work.
